WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:03.120
- I have a lot of stuff
going on in my life like,

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.340
that I don't like, heroin like,

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.219
eliminates a lot of the emotions for me,

00:00:07.219 --> 00:00:09.140
so I don't have to feel it.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.160
Like my daughter being gone

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.270
is one of the big, big
problems right now for me.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.370
And it really messed me up in the head

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:16.550
when they took her.

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:18.690
So like, that's why I use like that

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.613
because it just I don't have
to feel those feelings like.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.200
- [Mark] Okay, Cameron.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.900
So, I found you here on Skid Row

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.120
on the sidewalk this morning.
- Mm-hmm. Yes.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.120
- [Mark] Where'd you sleep last night?

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.140
- Mainly out, well,

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.571
I have a friend who has an
apartment down here a bit.

00:00:36.571 --> 00:00:39.170
Since I'm in search
for a person right now,

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:42.720
I'm kinda staying outside
so I don't miss him.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:43.620
Can't miss any second of it

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.066
'cause he could walk by any
moment I turn around, so--

00:00:47.066 --> 00:00:48.810
- [Mark] And where, and
you're from San Luis Obispo?

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:49.643
- Mm-hmm.

00:00:49.643 --> 00:00:50.870
- [Mark] Which is central, close to--

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:52.880
- Yeah, the Central Coast,

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.430
that's where I was raised out there.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:00.133
I was around on the east
coast for the past like,

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:02.820
been here for four years,

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.310
but before that I was on the east coast

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:05.199
for about eight years.

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:06.032
- [Mark] And what were
you doing back there?

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:09.030
- Just moving around and
working and stuff like that.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.931
- [Mark] What kind of work have you done?

00:01:10.931 --> 00:01:13.870
- I've done anything from retail

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:17.380
to working for Verizon
commercials in New York City.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.273
Stuff like that.

00:01:18.273 --> 00:01:19.880
Just kind of bounce around jobs.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.947
I kind of know little bit of everything,

00:01:22.947 --> 00:01:24.293
so that's always a plus.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.103
- [Mark] What age did
you start doing drugs?

00:01:28.103 --> 00:01:29.853
- [Cameron] I think I started well,

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:32.908
I used to smoke weed a lot like,

00:01:32.908 --> 00:01:34.663
that started around eighth grade.

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:38.570
But I didn't really like dabble into like,

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.930
the harder stuff until
like, I was about 19 or 20.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:43.050
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.400
- [Cameron] And then I took a break

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.460
from it for a long time,
I ended up having a kid,

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.563
and she's six now.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.261
- [Mark] Where is she?

00:01:52.261 --> 00:01:56.200
- [Cameron] She was taken
from me like two years ago.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.180
CPS wrongfully took her from me.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:00.000
- [Mark] The state took her away?

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.210
- [Cameron] Yeah, over some ridiculous

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:03.880
like, they weren't supposed to take her,

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:08.350
but they weren't gonna
listen to me so, you know?

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.910
But I haven't seen her in about two years.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:11.760
- [Mark] Ah, that's sad.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.223
- [Cameron] Yeah. I miss her.

00:02:14.249 --> 00:02:16.230
But I'm figuring all that stuff out now.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.300
I just I got carried
away with a lot of stuff

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.960
and messed up, and I know I did though,

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.360
at least I'm not in denial of it, so.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.730
I'm working on a lot
of stuff right now, so.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:27.390
- [Mark] Yeah. It's a struggle.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.223
- [Cameron] Yeah, it is.

00:02:28.223 --> 00:02:29.960
I got a lot of stuff going on, but.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.290
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:34.123
- [Mark] And down here on Skid Row,

00:02:34.123 --> 00:02:35.420
a lot of the girls are

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:38.860
getting into prostitution just to like--

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:39.945
- Yeah.
- Pay for things?

00:02:39.945 --> 00:02:42.140
- [Cameron] Oh, there's,
there's quite a handful of them.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.525
That's further down that way actually.

00:02:43.525 --> 00:02:44.680
- [Mark] Yeah, you
haven't gotten with that?

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.610
- [Cameron] No, I can't
bring myself to do it.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:47.650
I don't know.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:50.040
I, people either think I do it

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:53.230
or have offered for me to do it.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.400
I can't bring myself to do it though.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.040
- Mm-hmm.
- It's not just for,

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.950
like, I'm watching what happens

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.977
to these other girls down
here makes me really sad.

00:03:00.977 --> 00:03:02.173
But I mean that's their hustle, you know?

00:03:02.173 --> 00:03:03.984
I respect them. I respect
what they do, but--

00:03:03.984 --> 00:03:04.817
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:05.742
- It's not for everybody.

00:03:05.742 --> 00:03:07.670
- [Mark] They're making,
they're making ends meet.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.610
- Mm-hmm.
- Doing whatever they can.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:10.610
- Yeah, that's true.

00:03:12.476 --> 00:03:15.266
But me, nah, I've never, I couldn't.

00:03:15.266 --> 00:03:16.742
I don't know.

00:03:16.742 --> 00:03:18.770
Never really put it past myself

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:22.640
to try doing that for whatever.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.720
- [Mark] Where would you like
to see yourself in five years?

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:25.833
- Five years?

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:28.420
Probably living out in the Bay Area

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:29.778
'cause I like it a lot up there.

00:03:29.778 --> 00:03:31.620
- [Mark] Mm-hmm.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.950
- Only because I do a lot of art.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:37.294
And I'm in, I do tattooing,
and I do painting, so.

00:03:37.294 --> 00:03:40.400
That's like my getaway from all this,

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.850
and the stress and stuff, so.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.260
I think that's where I like
to see myself in five years.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.560
And I know I can do it so,

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.670
I'm gonna try really hard.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:53.382
Starting now, like,
this year get to there.

00:03:53.382 --> 00:03:54.215
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:54.215 --> 00:03:58.004
- But yeah, I'm just, it's
not a happy place down here.

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.178
- No.
- No, like--

00:03:59.178 --> 00:04:00.147
Every time I come down here,

00:04:00.147 --> 00:04:01.550
I'm just like this puts me

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:04.163
in such a bummer mood every time.

00:04:04.163 --> 00:04:05.473
I don't want to feel these feelings,

00:04:05.473 --> 00:04:08.583
like it's hard for me to
have to deal without that.

00:04:08.583 --> 00:04:09.913
That is why I use it.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:12.484
It just helps.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:17.100
But it's something that I'm
trying to look past like,

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.700
I'm eventually I'm gonna start a program,

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.640
like I think I might look into more.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:23.830
I did this month, like a couple weeks ago,

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.770
I looked into programs,

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:27.743
but I think I'm gonna start really like,

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:31.050
moving towards not just looking into them,

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:32.990
but like maybe like getting into one.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:33.823
- [Mark] Mm-hmm.

00:04:33.823 --> 00:04:36.590
Like, I wouldn't mind doing like,

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:37.860
an intensive outpatient treatment.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.100
Just because I know I
have other shit to do,

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.020
I can't just stay indoors,

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:45.330
and like be there locked up to get clean.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.860
Like I couldn't do that,
it would drive me nuts.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:50.320
I'd have to be able to go do other things,

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.413
and safely and like,

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:55.560
it's kind of like a
willpower type of thing,

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:58.130
like I'd feel more accomplished
if I was able to like,

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.970
maintain me being sober

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.101
and being able to do stuff
on the outside, you know?

00:05:03.101 --> 00:05:05.410
- [Mark] I mean, sometimes the pull

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:08.820
must be so strong, you just can't--

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.010
- Sometimes.
- You can't resist, right?

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.830
- Yeah, but that's when it all comes down

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.710
to whether like you know you
can really do it or you can't,

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:20.430
like, and obviously
I've gone clean before.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:23.510
And I went without it for
like almost 12 years like.

00:05:24.527 --> 00:05:25.360
And I did it by myself,

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:26.730
I didn't need help from, you know,

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:30.270
a patient treatment center
or, you know, a doctor.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.420
I just did it myself, like.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:33.910
You know, that first month was hell,

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.270
and like, I suffered for it but, you know,

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:38.120
I put myself there, like nothing ever,

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.330
like drugs that good, if
you think they're that good,

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.480
like nothing that good
is ever going to come

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.098
without a price.

00:05:44.098 --> 00:05:45.670
And like whether it's
going through withdrawal

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:47.870
and like, feeling all that,

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.810
like, that's the price you have to pay

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.837
if you're gonna, you know, mess
around with stuff like that.

00:05:51.837 --> 00:05:53.405
- [Mark] That goes for
everything, not just drugs.

00:05:53.405 --> 00:05:55.216
- Yeah, that's everything for sure.

00:05:55.216 --> 00:05:56.049
- [Mark] Absolutely.

00:05:56.049 --> 00:05:58.130
- But especially for drugs like,

00:05:58.130 --> 00:05:59.470
that the consequences are there,

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:01.260
you just have to know
whether you can handle it,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.665
or not, you know?

00:06:02.665 --> 00:06:05.056
And that's, that's how I see
it at least, I don't know,

00:06:05.056 --> 00:06:06.650
but I know I can do it,
it's just a matter of me

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:09.710
just conjuring up the
strength to get out there

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:12.300
and just do it and stop
making excuses for myself.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.370
Why I shouldn't do it like,

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.930
that's the only thing
I'm working on right now,

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.930
but I've come a long way,

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:19.890
so I'm getting a lot better.

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:20.846
- [Mark] Well, good luck.

00:06:20.846 --> 00:06:21.914
- [Cameron] Thank you.

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:22.920
- [Mark] Thank you for talking to me.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.008
- [Cameron] You're welcome. Thank you.

00:06:24.008 --> 00:06:24.850
Thank you for talking to me.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:26.609
It actually made me feel
better this morning,

00:06:26.609 --> 00:06:27.810
fucking standing there
getting all frustrated

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:29.210
with fucking all this stuff.

